package main

// ❌ OLD (as a pattern to avoid in Go): spawning one thread per
// connection. Each connection consumes a full OS thread (MB of stack
// + OS scheduling), so 10k concurrent connections needs 10k threads —
// the OS and memory quickly cap out, and thread context switching
// dominates. Many classic servers hit this wall.

// In Go, the equivalent WRONG pattern is spawning a goroutine that
// BLOCKS on a syscall directly (rare), or using cgo calls that block.
// Normal Go socket I/O is already non-blocking via the netpoller.

